  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the set $X={r,s,t,u,v,x,y,z}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n{{r,u,z},{s,t,y},\\,____\\,}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $r\\in {r,u,z}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $s\\in {s,t,y}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $t\\in {s,t,y}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $u\\in {r,u,z}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $v$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $x$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y\\in {s,t,y}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $z\\in {r,u,z}\\,\u2713$\n\nThe elements $v$ and $x$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${v,x}.$",
